Subject: [PATCH 66/75] =?UTF-8?q?fix(polecat):=20resolve=20agent-bead=20re?=
 =?UTF-8?q?claim=20wedge=20=E2=80=94=20read=20cleanup=5Fstatus=20from=20to?=
 =?UTF-8?q?wn=20store=20+=20reconcile=20empty/done?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Polecat agent beads (and their cleanup_status) are canonically stored in the
town db: every mutation — gt done's UpdateAgentCleanupStatus, check-recovery's
--reconcile-cleanup, GetAgentBead — routes through ForAgentBead()/agentBeadTarget().
But the scheduler capacity snapshot (polecatCapacitySnapshotForTownNoCleanup) and
`gt polecat list` read them via the UNROUTED beads.New(rigPath).ListAgentBeads(),
a different store that never sees those writes. So a done polecat with a
clean/reconciled cleanup_status reads as missing here, is classified
NEEDS_RECOVERY, counted recovery_blocked, and occupies a slot — Free drops. Once
every polecat lands in that state the scheduler reclaims nothing and ready work
starves: the reclaim wedge. Route both reads through ForAgentBead() so capacity
and list see the same agent state everything writes. (GetAgentBead already routes;
ListAgentBeads intentionally does not — other callers compare town vs rig — so we
route at the two polecat-inventory call sites, not the shared method.)

Also harden cleanupStatusReconcileCandidate, which heals a stale cleanup_status
when live predicates prove SAFE_TO_NUKE: it previously skipped empty/missing
status and non-idle (done) polecats, so a completed polecat whose status was
cleared by ResetAgentBeadForReuse could never be reconciled to clean. Reconcile
empty the same as dirty, and accept StateDone (awaiting reclaim); the SAFE_TO_NUKE
verdict gate still rejects any still-working polecat.

Validated live: done polecats now classify reusable_idle (recovery: 0) and the
queue dispatches by reclaiming them instead of wedging.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
